      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:7:7:13",
      "text": [
        " كُلُّ يَمِينٍ لَا يُرَادُ بِهَا وَجْهُ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى فِي طَلَاقٍ أَوْ عِتْقٍ فَلَيْسَ بِشَيْ‏ءٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Safwan, from Ibn Muskan, from Al Halby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Every oath not intended for the Sake of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> the High, regarding a divorce or freeing a slave, so it is not with anything’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "13. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Safwan from ibn Muskan from al-Halabiy who has narrated the following: “Abu ‘ Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Any oath which is not for the sake of Allah, most High, in divorce or freeing slaves does not have any valid effect.’” "
        ]
      }
